  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Wu Yong says Gu Immortal Yan Huang challenged Yu Bo because Xia clan is after Moon Bowl, one of Wu clan’s most important resource points that produces moon path Gu worms. Moon Bowl is not a bowl; it is a valley with a peculiar bowl shape, called Moon Bowl because it produces moon path Gu worms. A village once stood in it with a Gu Immortal known as Immortal Yan Huang. When Wu clan expanded it eradicated the village to take Moon Bowl, and as a righteous path clan it needed a proper reason rather than killing Yan Huang outright. Yan Huang later stakes Moon Bowl in a challenge to Wu Yu Bo: whoever wins obtains Moon Bowl. After Wu clan loses, Fang Yuan tells Xia Qing Cang the battle is over and Moon Bowl is theirs.",
      "chapters": [
        1303
      ],
